---
/*
  Home. Structure and copy: 04-konzept.md section 4.3, page "/".
  Six sections, one message above the fold, no number tiles, no badges.

  PENDING DECISION 1 (Manuel): section "What it costs, before you ask" states
  the split publicly. The concept recommends it, Manuel has not signed it off.
  PENDING DECISION 2 (Manuel): the contract term sentence in the same section.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import RecordCard from '../components/RecordCard.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { legal } from '../site';

const records = (await getCollection('records'))
  .filter((entry) => !entry.data.draft)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const firstRecord = records[0];
---

<Base
  title="Wunder | Managed against your own numbers"
  description="Wunder is a creator management company registered in Riga. We write down what your account did on its own over the last thirty days, and everything after that is measured against that number."
>
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <h1>Managed against your own numbers.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Wunder is a creator management company registered in Riga. Before we start, we write
            down what your account did on its own over the last thirty days. Everything we do after
            that is measured against that number, in the same portal you log into.
          </p>
          <CtaBlock secondary />
        </div>
        <Placeholder label="Own production photography" ratio="portrait" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>You know what your account did at its best.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        We write that number down before we start, and we let you measure us against it.
      </p>
      {
        firstRecord && (
          <div class="record-slot">
            <RecordCard {...firstRecord.data} />
          </div>
        )
      }
      <p class="caption">
        Every result on this site is one case, dated, with the part that did not work written next
        to it. <a href="/proof">See how we report numbers</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The reason you are reading this page.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Almost everyone who ends up on a call with us is looking for one of four things: growth
        that has stalled on its own, someone to take on the parts of the work that are not the
        content itself, marketing knowledge they have not had to build themselves, or time back.
        We are not going to guess which one is yours. Tell us on the call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Three things we can show you, not just tell you.</h2>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>You see the same screen we do</h3>
          <p>
            Every post runs through our own posting system, and we read every number at the source
            instead of estimating it. You log into your own portal and see views, reach and
            followers over seven, thirty and ninety days.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/how-it-works#portal">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>You never hand us a password</h3>
          <p>
            Instagram publishing runs through Zernio, the OnlyFans chat and vault work runs through
            Infloww, both authorised interfaces. A permission you granted can be withdrawn. A
            password you handed over cannot.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/how-it-works#access">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>The people writing in your name get audited</h3>
          <p>
            Twice a week an automated run pulls the last finished shift and scores it against a
            versioned rubric. The run is on a schedule and nobody on the chat team can switch it
            off.
          </p>
          <p>
            Who writes to your fans is written down, not just told to you. You are free to say so
            in your own bio. If you want a line about it there, we will not ask you to remove it.
          </p>
          <p><a href="/how-it-works#chatting">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What it costs, before you ask.</h2>
      <p>
        The split is 50/50. No setup fee, no minimum revenue. OnlyFans pays out to your own account
        first. We invoice our share afterwards, once a week.
      </p>
      <p>
        [Pending decision, Manuel and Lauris] The agreement runs six months and then renews for six
        months unless someone cancels. From month two on, either side can cancel any time in
        writing, effective at the end of that month, no reason required. The same notice period
        applies to us, and we send you a reminder six weeks before the term would otherwise renew,
        naming the exact date and the address the cancellation goes to.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your content stays yours. We never held your passwords, so there is nothing to hand back
        except portal access, which we switch off the same day.
      </p>
      <p class="caption">
        Conditions on this page are pending sign off. See the note in the pull request.
      </p>
      <CtaBlock />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>A registered company, with two people who sign for it.</h2>
      <p>
        Wunder is a brand by {legal.company}, registration number {legal.regNumber}, registered in
        Riga on {legal.registered}. Two managing directors, each with sole signing authority: Manuel
        Gonzalez, CEO and co owner, and Lauris Kalnins, COO and co owner.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can look that up before you talk to either of them. <a href="/company"
          >The company page has the rest</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Apply, and we will tell you either way.</h2>
      <p>
        You send eight short answers, a person reads them, and you get an answer whether it is a fit
        or not. If it is not, you get one sentence instead of silence.
      </p>
      <p>We answer within one working day.</p>
      <CtaBlock secondary />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 88px;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .record-slot {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 32px 0 24px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      padding-top: 48px;
    }
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
